  "claim": "Remove unused DVC and its exclusive dependency closure from the runtime; retain all surviving distribution versions and archive metadata. The pinned OSV-Scanner reproduces the advisory before removal and passes both exhaustive CI inventory groups afterward.",
  "advisory": {
    "id": "PYSEC-2026-2447",
    "aliases": [
      "GHSA-w8v5-vhqr-4h9v",
      "CVE-2025-69872"
    ],
    "affected": "diskcache <=5.6.3; OSV range introduced 0, last_affected 5.6.3; no fixed event",
    "path": "Cache.get/__getitem__ -> Disk.fetch in MODE_PICKLE -> pickle.load; cache-key decoding also uses pickle.load in Disk.get.",
    "trigger": "An attacker must write a crafted pickle to the SQLite cache or value file before the victim reads it. The default Disk implementation has no deserialization allowlist.",
    "impact": "Code execution in the cache reader process, if those attacker-write and victim-read conditions hold.",
    "assessment": "Confirmed package/advisory match. Runtime exploitability was not demonstrated; the recipe only imports DVC, and no DVC cache operation is called. Removal avoids depending on a reachability exception.",
    "poc_sketch": "Attacker with cache write access inserts a pickle whose reduce operation selects a callable; victim Cache.get reads MODE_PICKLE data; Disk.fetch calls pickle.load, invoking that callable. No exploit payload was executed.",
    "sources": [
      "https://api.osv.dev/v1/vulns/PYSEC-2026-2447",
      "https://api.osv.dev/v1/vulns/GHSA-w8v5-vhqr-4h9v",
      "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w8v5-vhqr-4h9v",
      "https://github.com/EthanKim88/ethan-cve-disclosures/blob/main/CVE-2025-69872-DiskCache-Pickle-Deserialization.md",
      "https://github.com/grantjenks/python-diskcache/blob/323787f507a6456c56cce213156a78b17073fe00/diskcache/core.py#L165-L177",
